&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;COMMUNICATIONS LEAD, WIKIMEDIA ENTERPRISE (CONTRACT)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Contract terms:&lt;/strong&gt; 40 hours/week, initial 6-month contract, with potential to extend based on organizational needs&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Reports to: &lt;/strong&gt;Communications Manager (dotted line to President of Wikimedia Enterprise)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Summary&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Wikimedia Foundation is the nonprofit that operates Wikipedia and the other Wikimedia free knowledge projects. Our mission is to bring free educational content to the world.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Wikimedia Enterprise is the Wikimedia Foundation&#39;s commercial product for large-scale reusers and distributors of Wikimedia content. Through Enterprise agreements, companies gain improved, commercial-grade access to Wikimedia content at a volume and scale they need,&amp;nbsp; while directly supporting the Wikimedia Foundation&#39;s free knowledge mission. As AI systems increasingly scrape Wikipedia at scale, Wikimedia Enterprise has become critical to a sustainable model for Wikimedia projects and the open knowledge ecosystem.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for an experienced communications lead to serve as the primary communications partner to the Wikimedia Enterprise team — shaping external messaging, media relations, and thought leadership to drive organic demand for Wikimedia Enterprise services, while ensuring narrative and strategic alignment with the Foundation&#39;s broader communications priorities.&amp;nbsp; This role sits in the Media Relations team, within the Foundation’s &lt;a href=&quot;https://meta.wikimedia.org/wiki/Wikimedia_Foundation/Communications&quot;&gt;Communications Department&lt;/a&gt;, with a dotted line to the President of Wikimedia Enterprise.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and own the external communications strategy for Wikimedia Enterprise across media/trade press, speaking engagements, and other channels that build visibility and organic demand for Enterprise offerings.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build relationships with reporters (mainstream and B2B tech trade press) and conference organizers to secure speaking opportunities and position Wikimedia Enterprise as the go-to product for commercial content reusers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as a primary media liaison for Wikimedia Enterprise, working with the wider media relations team to manage daily press inquiries, prepping spokespeople/staffing interviews, information requests, and speaking engagement requests in a timely manner. This includes leading rapid response media efforts — triaging sensitive, fast-moving situations with sound judgment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with internal teams to develop narratives and thought leadership that strengthens Wikimedia Enterprise&#39;s brand relevance and positioning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Guide, produce, and review marketing and communications materials — press statements, blogs, pitch notes and lists, briefing docs, and more — ensuring key messages about Wikimedia Enterprise are shaped consistently and clearly for public audiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate&amp;nbsp; the end-to-end communications workflow for major external launches and announcements together with the Enterprise Growth team, from drafting through internal review, stakeholder approvals, and release.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure alignment between the Wikimedia Enterprise growth plan and the Foundation&#39;s annual communications calendar.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build relationships and lead cooperative efforts with internal and external stakeholders — Wikimedia Foundation colleagues, Wikimedia volunteers and affiliates, and external partners — to enable the successful delivery of communications plans.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage relationships with external vendors (such as PR agencies) as directed to deliver on goals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use data and customer insights to refine messaging, content, and strategy for Wikimedia Enterprise across business audiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with leadership to set goals and KPIs for Wikimedia Enterprise communications, track results against the growth plan, and share actionable insights with leadership and key stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Skills and experience&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;At least 8+ years of communications experience, including experience operating at a senior/lead level with minimal oversight in a tech and/or B2B tech environment or supporting a commercial product line.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience bridging communications and marketing/growth functions — ideally in a role that required translating between brand/editorial priorities and commercial or growth objectives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with developing and executing earned media strategy and thought leadership, building relationships with press, partners, and wider stakeholders to develop a pipeline of coverage across channels and platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent stakeholder management skills, including experience influencing senior and executive stakeholders, with a track record of working effectively across teams with different priorities, cultures, and reporting lines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sound judgment on reputational risk and sensitivity, particularly when balancing commercial messaging against mission-driven or community-facing considerations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable operating with ambiguity, with the ability to ramp up quickly and take ownership of a live workflow with minimal onboarding, given the fixed-term nature of this role.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong writing and editing skills, with the ability to adapt tone across formats — from press materials to marketing copy to internal briefing documents.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong editorial judgment: demonstrable ability to review and shape marketing materials (campaigns, web copy, social, blogs, thought leadership) for voice, tone, and brand consistency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of tying communications to business results: setting metrics, measuring impact (coverage quality, share of voice, inbound demand, pipeline influence) and changing course based on the data.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in a matrixed organization, comfortable with dotted-line reporting and leading through influence and collaboration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working remotely and across multiple time zones and emerging markets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience overseeing and managing relationships with external agencies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in a nonprofit, open-source, mission-driven, or community-governed organization, especially one with a commercial or earned-revenue arm.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Real understanding of AI, how it works, data licensing and content provenance debates&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with the Wikimedia movement, Wikipedia, or free-knowledge/open-content spaces.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background in tech, media, or platform companies navigating AI-related content, licensing, or data issues.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;About the Wikimedia Foundation&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Wikimedia Foundation is the nonprofit organization that operates Wikipedia and the other Wikimedia free knowledge projects. Our vision is a world in which every single human can freely share in the sum of all knowledge. We believe that everyone has the potential to contribute something to our shared knowledge, and that everyone should be able to access that knowledge freely. We host Wikipedia and the Wikimedia projects, build software experiences for reading, contributing, and sharing Wikimedia content, support the volunteer communities and partners who make Wikimedia possible, and advocate for policies that enable Wikimedia and free knowledge to thrive.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Wikimedia Foundation is a charitable, not-for-profit organization that relies on donations. We receive donations from millions of individuals around the world, with an average donation of about $15. We also receive donations through institutional grants and gifts. The Wikimedia Foundation is a United States 501(c)(3) tax-exempt organization with offices in San Francisco, California, USA.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;strong&gt;As an equal opportunity employer, the Wikimedia Foundation values having a diverse workforce and continuously strives to maintain an inclusive and equitable workplace. We encourage people with a diverse range of backgrounds to apply. We do not discriminate against any person based upon their race, traits historically associated with race, religion, color, national origin, sex, pregnancy or related medical conditions, parental status, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, age, status as a protected veteran, status as an individual with a disability, genetic information, or any other legally protected characteristics.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Wikimedia Foundation is a remote-first organization with staff members including contractors based 40+ countries&lt;strong&gt;*&lt;/strong&gt;. Salaries at the Wikimedia Foundation are set in a way that is competitive, equitable, and consistent with our values and culture. The anticipated annual pay range of this position for applicants based within the United States is US$&lt;span data-sheets-root=&quot;1&quot;&gt;118,361&lt;/span&gt; to US$&lt;span data-sheets-root=&quot;1&quot;&gt;182,658 &lt;/span&gt;with multiple individualized factors, including cost of living in the location, being the determinants of the offered pay. For applicants located outside of the US, the pay range will be adjusted to the country of hire. We neither ask for nor take into consideration the salary history of applicants. The compensation for a successful applicant will be based on their skills, experience and location.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;*Please note that we are currently able to hire in the following:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;US States&lt;/strong&gt;: Arizona, California, Colorado, Connecticut, District of Columbia*, Florida, Georgia, Idaho, Illinois, Indiana, Iowa, Maryland, Massachusetts, Michigan, Minnesota, Missouri, New Jersey, New Mexico, New York, North Carolina, Ohio, Oklahoma, Oregon, Pennsylvania, Puerto Rico*, Rhode Island, Tennessee, Texas, Utah, Vermont, Virginia, Washington, West Virginia, Wisconsin and Wyoming (*US Territory or Federal District)&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Countries: &lt;/strong&gt;Brazil, Canada, Colombia, France, Germany, Ghana, India, Indonesia, Italy, Kenya*, Mexico, Morocco, Netherlands, Poland, Singapore*, South Africa, Spain, Switzerland and the United Kingdom. Our non-US employees are hired through a local third party Employer of Record (EOR) and must have current work authorization in their location. (&lt;em&gt;*citizens/permanent residents only)&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We periodically review this list to streamline to ensure alignment with our hiring requirements.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;All applicants can reach out to their recruiter to understand more about the specific pay range for their location during the interview process.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;strong&gt;If you are a qualified applicant requiring assistance or an accommodation to complete any step of the application process due to a disability, you may contact us at recruiting@wikimedia.org or +1 (415) 839-6885.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;More information&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1;&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://foundation.wikimedia.org/wiki/Applicant_privacy_policy&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Applicant Privacy Policy&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1;&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://wikimediafoundation.org/&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Wikimedia Foundation&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1;&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=8mvPYF_erNA&amp;amp;list=PLVx9pX-VnGVh9Akb-O-SAKZ-GDTVTHZqS&amp;amp;index=8&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What does the Wikimedia Foundation do?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1;&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=7gATwhhGrPk&amp;amp;list=PLVx9pX-VnGVh9Akb-O-SAKZ-GDTVTHZqS&amp;amp;index=1&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What makes Wikipedia different from social media platforms?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1;&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://wikimediafoundation.org/wiki/Our_projects&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Projects&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1;&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://techblog.wikimedia.org/&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Tech Stack&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1;&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://wikimediafoundation.org/news/&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;News from across the Wikimedia movement&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1;&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://diff.wikimedia.org/&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Wikimedia Blog&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1;&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://meta.wikimedia.org/wiki/Strategy/Wikimedia_movement/2017&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Wikimedia 2030&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div id=&quot;l-content&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The Wikimedia Foundation is seeking a Community Management Associate to engage online communities, help refine our brand voice, and build a vibrant, Gen Z-focused social media presence for Wikipedia and the Wikimedia Foundation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Sitting on the Social Team within External Communications, you will bring energy and creativity to how we show up across platforms. From writing engaging comment copy and jumping on real-time cultural moments to surfacing stories from our global volunteer community, you will help connect Wikipedia with next-generation internet audiences.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a fast-moving, hands-on role perfect for someone who lives on social media, loves online culture, and is eager to test and learn. Preferred working time zones are UTC -8 to UTC -5 (Mexico, Columbia, Canada and United States)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ideally You Are:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A Digital Culture Native:&lt;/strong&gt; Plugged into emerging trends and short-form video culture (TikTok, Instagram Reels, YouTube Shorts) with a natural feel for Gen Z engagement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A Strong Communicator:&lt;/strong&gt; Experienced in writing social comment copy and adapting brand tone across different platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;An Organized Framework Builder:&lt;/strong&gt; Eager to help draft clear community playbooks, response protocols, and engagement guidelines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A Community Connector:&lt;/strong&gt; Excited to interact directly with followers and surface stories from our global volunteer network.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A Data-Aware Learner:&lt;/strong&gt; Comfortable reviewing basic analytics and social listening insights to refine engagement tactics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Community Engagement &amp;amp; Copywriting&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist in writing daily social copy, managing comment sections, and executing reactive engagement on trending moments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the development and documentation of community management playbooks and brand tone-of-voice guidelines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help identify, surface, and share inspiring stories from Wikipedia’s global volunteer community.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Trends &amp;amp; Growth&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track short-form video trends, platform updates, and emerging formats to recommend fresh engagement opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support testing of social listening and moderation tools to improve community response time.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Tracking &amp;amp; Operations&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor channel activity, track audience sentiment, and assist with monthly performance reporting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in creative experimentation to see which copy and engagement styles resonate best.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Skills &amp;amp; Experience&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;1–3 years&lt;/strong&gt; of hands-on experience in social media execution, community management, or digital storytelling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Short-Form Native:&lt;/strong&gt; Active familiarity with TikTok, Instagram Reels, and YouTube Shorts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Writing &amp;amp; Moderation:&lt;/strong&gt; Experience writing social copy, engaging in comment sections, or moderating online channels.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Basic Tool Familiarity:&lt;/strong&gt; Exposure to social management, analytics, or listening tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Good Judgment:&lt;/strong&gt; High emotional intelligence to navigate sensitive comments and know when to escalate risks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Global Mindset:&lt;/strong&gt; Awareness of cross-cultural nuances and working with diverse global audiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualities That Matter to Us&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Passion for the Wikimedia mission and free knowledge.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexibility working with distributed teams across time zones.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A collaborative spirit, curiosity, and a real love for internet culture.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;About the Wikimedia Foundation&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Wikimedia Foundation is the nonprofit organization that operates Wikipedia and the other Wikimedia free knowledge projects. Our vision is a world in which every single human can freely share in the sum of all knowledge. We believe that everyone has the potential to contribute something to our shared knowledge, and that everyone should be able to access that knowledge freely. We host Wikipedia and the Wikimedia projects, build software experiences for reading, contributing, and sharing Wikimedia content, support the volunteer communities and partners who make Wikimedia possible, and advocate for policies that enable Wikimedia and free knowledge to thrive.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Wikimedia Foundation is a charitable, not-for-profit organization that relies on donations. We receive donations from millions of individuals around the world, with an average donation of about $15. We also receive donations through institutional grants and gifts. The Wikimedia Foundation is a United States 501(c)(3) tax-exempt organization with offices in San Francisco, California, USA.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;strong&gt;As an equal opportunity employer, the Wikimedia Foundation values having a diverse workforce and continuously strives to maintain an inclusive and equitable workplace. We encourage people with a diverse range of backgrounds to apply. We do not discriminate against any person based upon their race, traits historically associated with race, religion, color, national origin, sex, pregnancy or related medical conditions, parental status, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, age, status as a protected veteran, status as an individual with a disability, genetic information, or any other legally protected characteristics.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Wikimedia Foundation is a remote-first organization with staff members including contractors based 40+ countries&lt;strong&gt;*&lt;/strong&gt;. Salaries at the Wikimedia Foundation are set in a way that is competitive, equitable, and consistent with our values and culture. The anticipated annual pay range of this position for applicants based within the United States is US$62,074 to US$93,077 with multiple individualized factors, including cost of living in the location, being the determinants of the offered pay. For applicants located outside of the US, the pay range will be adjusted to the country of hire. We neither ask for nor take into consideration the salary history of applicants. The compensation for a successful applicant will be based on their skills, experience and location.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;*Please note that we are currently able to hire in the following:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;US States&lt;/strong&gt;: Arizona, California, Colorado, Connecticut, District of Columbia*, Florida, Georgia, Idaho, Illinois, Indiana, Iowa, Maryland, Massachusetts, Michigan, Minnesota, Missouri, New Jersey, New Mexico, New York, North Carolina, Ohio, Oklahoma, Oregon, Pennsylvania, Puerto Rico*, Rhode Island, Tennessee, Texas, Utah, Vermont, Virginia, Washington, West Virginia, Wisconsin and Wyoming (*US Territory or Federal District)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;For US-based applicants: this position is part of the Communication Workers of America bargaining unit.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Countries: &lt;/strong&gt;Brazil, Canada, Colombia, France, Germany, Ghana, India, Indonesia, Italy, Kenya*, Mexico, Morocco, Netherlands, Poland, Singapore*, South Africa, Spain, Switzerland and the United Kingdom. Our non-US employees are hired through a local third party Employer of Record (EOR) and must have current work authorization in their location. (&lt;em&gt;*citizens/permanent residents only)&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;We periodically review this list to streamline to ensure alignment with our hiring requirements.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;All applicants can reach out to their recruiter to understand more about the specific pay range for their location during the interview process.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;strong&gt;If you are a qualified applicant requiring assistance or an accommodation to complete any step of the application process due to a disability, you may contact us at recruiting@wikimedia.org or +1 (415) 839-6885.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;More information&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1;&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://wikimediafoundation.org/about/jobs/#section-12&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;U.S. Benefits &amp;amp; Perks&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1;&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://foundation.wikimedia.org/wiki/Applicant_privacy_policy&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Applicant Privacy Policy&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1;&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://wikimediafoundation.org/&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Wikimedia Foundation&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1;&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=8mvPYF_erNA&amp;amp;list=PLVx9pX-VnGVh9Akb-O-SAKZ-GDTVTHZqS&amp;amp;index=8&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What does the Wikimedia Foundation do?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1;&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=7gATwhhGrPk&amp;amp;list=PLVx9pX-VnGVh9Akb-O-SAKZ-GDTVTHZqS&amp;amp;index=1&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What makes Wikipedia different from social media platforms?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1;&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://wikimediafoundation.org/wiki/Our_projects&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Projects&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1;&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://techblog.wikimedia.org/&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Tech Stack&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1;&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://wikimediafoundation.org/news/&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;News from across the Wikimedia movement&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1;&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://diff.wikimedia.org/&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Wikimedia Blog&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1;&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://meta.wikimedia.org/wiki/Strategy/Wikimedia_movement/2017&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Wikimedia 2030&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div id=&quot;l-content&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Summary&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Wikipedia and its sister projects are among the most popular media properties in the world, visited by over 1 billion people a month across over 300 different languages. These sites generate a tremendous amount of data on how people learn and collaborate.&amp;nbsp; The Wikimedia Foundation is looking for a group product manager to guide the development and evolution of our &lt;a href=&quot;https://wikitech.wikimedia.org/wiki/Data_Platform&quot;&gt;data platforms&lt;/a&gt;, the collection of technologies we use to understand how Wikipedia works, improve its experiences, and spread free knowledge.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The group product manager is a leader in the strategic decision-making and tactical execution for the Data Engineering, Experimentation, Search, and Data Platform Site Reliability teams. This role shares leadership responsibility with the Director of Engineering for Data Platform Engineering, and works in collaboration with data analysts, researchers, and product teams building user-facing features for reading and editing Wikipedia on the web and mobile apps. This is a people management role, managing two individually-contributing product managers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, you and your group of product managers will guide the evolution of our data pipelines, data lake, experiment platform, and analytics tools.&amp;nbsp; This includes ingestion, orchestration, computation, and serving data using a variety of technologies such as Kafka, Flink, Hadoop, Spark, Airflow, Iceberg, Kubernetes, Superset, dbt, and OpenSearch. A strong candidate will have deep experience building a data platform to serve product analytics and production needs, and be technically conversant in the relevant technologies.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This position will report to the Senior Director of Product, Core Experiences.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Candidates must be available for critical meetings and synchronous work between 15:00 UTC and 18:00 UTC, and open to traveling internationally up to four times per year.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;This role is accountable for:&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensuring the accuracy, usefulness, reliability, and accessibility of our data products&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Defining and setting priorities and roadmaps for Data Platform Engineering teams across four domains: data engineering, search, experimentation, and site reliability&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Product lifecycle management of the products, services, and tools of the Data Platform Engineering teams&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Co-developing product strategy, providing leadership, and making and facilitating sound decisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Managing and developing a team of product managers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partnering with user-facing product teams to use the data platform to guide product decisions and build derived-data products&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Expected skills and experience include:&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Minimum of 5 years of product management experience with data or infrastructure products&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience hiring and managing product managers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Success delivering data and analytical products and services depended on by multiple product teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expertise in data analytics, A/B testing, search, and data architecture&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of modern techniques for handling high-scale data&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of search technologies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience navigating privacy issues around data collection, retention, and distribution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work with multiple stakeholder teams to deliver results through lateral influence and collaboration&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Qualities that are important to us:&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Commitment to the &lt;a href=&quot;https://wikimediafoundation.org/about/mission/#:~:text=The%20mission%20of%20the%20Wikimedia,disseminate%20it%20effectively%20and%20globally.&quot;&gt;mission&lt;/a&gt; and &lt;a href=&quot;https://wikimediafoundation.org/about/values/&quot;&gt;values&lt;/a&gt; of the Wikimedia Foundation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Effective at asynchronous communication in a distributed workplace&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Able to navigate and make decisions in circumstances with limited, incomplete, and conflicting information&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Focus on iterative delivery and minimum viability to provide value to customer teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Effective at clear, written communication for strategy, plans, roadmaps, and decisions, for a wide range of audiences including individual contributor engineers, volunteer contributors, and department leadership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Additionally, we would love it if you have:&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with open source, open data, or open knowledge communities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building products for multiple languages and geographies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with the integration of machine learning or artificial intelligence into web products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience editing Wikipedia or with the Wikipedia, Wikidata, or Wikimedia Commons communities or other collaborative enterprises&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Open source software development experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with MediaWiki&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;About the Wikimedia Foundation&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Wikimedia Foundation is the nonprofit organization that operates Wikipedia and the other Wikimedia free knowledge projects. Our vision is a world in which every single human can freely share in the sum of all knowledge. We believe that everyone has the potential to contribute something to our shared knowledge, and that everyone should be able to access that knowledge freely. We host Wikipedia and the Wikimedia projects, build software experiences for reading, contributing, and sharing Wikimedia content, support the volunteer communities and partners who make Wikimedia possible, and advocate for policies that enable Wikimedia and free knowledge to thrive.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Wikimedia Foundation is a charitable, not-for-profit organization that relies on donations. We receive donations from millions of individuals around the world, with an average donation of about $15. We also receive donations through institutional grants and gifts. The Wikimedia Foundation is a United States 501(c)(3) tax-exempt organization with offices in San Francisco, California, USA.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;strong&gt;As an equal opportunity employer, the Wikimedia Foundation values having a diverse workforce and continuously strives to maintain an inclusive and equitable workplace. We encourage people with a diverse range of backgrounds to apply. We do not discriminate against any person based upon their race, traits historically associated with race, religion, color, national origin, sex, pregnancy or related medical conditions, parental status, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, age, status as a protected veteran, status as an individual with a disability, genetic information, or any other legally protected characteristics.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Wikimedia Foundation is a remote-first organization with staff members including contractors based 40+ countries&lt;strong&gt;*&lt;/strong&gt;. Salaries at the Wikimedia Foundation are set in a way that is competitive, equitable, and consistent with our values and culture. The anticipated annual pay range of this position for applicants based within the United States is US$&lt;span data-sheets-root=&quot;1&quot;&gt;131,926 &lt;/span&gt;to US$&lt;span data-sheets-root=&quot;1&quot;&gt;206,302 &lt;/span&gt;with multiple individualized factors, including cost of living in the location, being the determinants of the offered pay. For applicants located outside of the US, the pay range will be adjusted to the country of hire. We neither ask for nor take into consideration the salary history of applicants. The compensation for a successful applicant will be based on their skills, experience and location.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;*Please note that we are currently able to hire in the following:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;US States&lt;/strong&gt;: Arizona, California, Colorado, Connecticut, District of Columbia*, Florida, Georgia, Idaho, Illinois, Indiana, Iowa, Maryland, Massachusetts, Michigan, Minnesota, Missouri, New Jersey, New Mexico, New York, North Carolina, Ohio, Oklahoma, Oregon, Pennsylvania, Puerto Rico*, Rhode Island, Tennessee, Texas, Utah, Vermont, Virginia, Washington, West Virginia, Wisconsin and Wyoming (*US Territory or Federal District)&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Countries: &lt;/strong&gt;Brazil, Canada, Colombia, Germany, Ghana, India, Indonesia, Italy, Kenya*, Mexico, Morocco, Netherlands, Poland, Singapore*, South Africa, Spain, Switzerland and the United Kingdom. Our non-US employees are hired through a local third party Employer of Record (EOR) and must have current work authorization in their location. (&lt;em&gt;*citizens/permanent residents only)&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;We periodically review this list to streamline to ensure alignment with our hiring requirements.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;All applicants can reach out to their recruiter to understand more about the specific pay range for their location during the interview process.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;strong&gt;If you are a qualified applicant requiring assistance or an accommodation to complete any step of the application process due to a disability, you may contact us at recruiting@wikimedia.org or +1 (415) 839-6885.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
